<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 13 August, from 1521 to 1961.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1521 CE <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tenochtitlan falls to Cortés and his allies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of nearly three months, Spanish forces and their Tlaxcalan allies captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc">Cuauhtémoc</a> and the Aztec capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a>, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>, rose on its ruins.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc">Cuauhtémoc</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1704 CE <span class="tih-ago">322 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marlborough and Prince Eugene win the Battle of Blenheim</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-churchill-1st-duke-of-marlborough">Duke of Marlborough</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-eugene-of-savoy">Prince Eugene of Savoy</a> destroyed a Franco-Bavarian army at Blenheim. The victory saved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> and knocked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1814 CE <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Netherlands cedes the Cape Colony to Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Convention of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, the Dutch formally ceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> had occupied since 1806. British rule shaped southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> for the following century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1898 CE <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US forces take Manila from Spain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> after a largely staged battle with the Spanish garrison, unaware that a peace protocol had been signed the day before. The US went on to annex the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1961 CE <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">East Germany seals the border in Berlin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Overnight, East German forces closed the crossings and began building barriers that became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a>. For 28 years it divided the city, and at least 140 people died trying to cross.</p></div></li></ol>
